<title>SINGAPORE: ANA Hotels surge on takeover rumours.</title>
<headline>ANA Hotels surge on takeover rumours.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Revived takeover rumours drove ANA Hotels shares up dramatically on the Singapore Stock Exchange on Wednesday, traders said.</p>
<p>By 0836 GMT, it had risen $0.56, or 18.67 percent, to S$3.56 on active trade of 109,000 shares.</p>
<p>&quot;It's the takeover fever. But I doubt the credibility of the rumour as the company is strongly backed by a Japanese government-related concern,&quot; said a dealer with a local institution.</p>
<p>&quot;It looks more likely to be an asset play,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>ANA hotels officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
